 "notes": [
  "Two-step questions. My home moves to another country (Bergen to Tampere). The boat's owner changes from my sister to my brother, and my dog's name from Ana to Otto. My cat's eye colour is said outright and also implied by a link to mine; my brother's city is only implied, by a link to my sister's. The tent belongs to my neighbour, of whom nothing else is taught.",
  "A chain asks about now. A name points at the one entity called that now. A link is read one way and one link deep, and only fills gaps: what is said outright wins. 'Or' is inclusive; compound questions use Kleene's three-valued logic. The country of a city is fixed general knowledge; its question ('Which country is Oslo in?') is asked in every phase, so chains the base model cannot finish can be dropped when scoring."
 ],
